pan style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">24</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">How many rectangles (squares included) are there in the given figure?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image008.png\" width=\"152\" height=\"151\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A rectangle is fixed by choosing </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">two upright lines</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">and </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">two level lines</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">There are 4 upright lines — any 2 of them:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4 × 3 ÷ 2 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> ways</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">There are 5 level lines — any 2 of them:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5 × 4 ÷ 2 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">10</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> ways</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Every such choice gives one rectangle:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">6 × 10 = </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">60</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 4 – 60</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50053", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V &lt; Q</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Q &gt; V</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V &gt; Q</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Q ≥ V</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">In the given statement, @ means &gt;, &amp; means &lt;, # means =, ! means ≥, % means ≤.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Statement: V # R @ U ! P @ Q</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Which of the given conclusions is definitely true?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Replace each symbol by the sign it stands for.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V = R &gt; U ≥ P &gt; Q</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Read the chain from V to Q.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Only </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">V &gt; Q</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> holds for every set of values</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">that fits the statement.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 3 – V &gt; Q</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50054", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">C</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">E</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">H</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Eight people — A, B, C, D, E, F, G and H — live on eight different floors of the same building, the lowest floor being numbered 1 and the topmost 8.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">G lives 3 floors above A.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">C lives on an even-numbered floor.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">F lives 4 floors above E.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">D lives 3 floors above H.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Only 3 people live above H.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">D lives 2 floors above C.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Who lives on floor 5?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Take the clues in the order given,</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">and see how far each one cuts the list down.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• G lives 3 floors above A. → 3600 still fit</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• C lives on an even-numbered floor. → 1800 still fit</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• F lives 4 floors above E. → 120 still fit</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• D lives 3 floors above H. → 12 still fit</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• Only 3 people live above H. → 2 still fit</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">• D lives 2 floors above C. → 1 still fit</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The one arrangement left, from the top floor down:</sp