ion": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Select the answer figure that is the correct mirror image of the question figure when the mirror is held along the right-hand side of the figure.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image010.png\" width=\"116\" height=\"116\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A mirror held at the </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">side</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> of a figure</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">swaps </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">left and right</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">and leaves top and bottom exactly as they are.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">So every part of the figure keeps its height</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">and moves across to the other half.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 2 — the figure turned upside down, which is a water image </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 3 — the figure rotated by a quarter turn </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 4 — the question figure itself </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 1</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50056", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The factory is now producing more usable output from the same work</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The new machines are faster than the old ones</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The workers have been trained better this year</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The old machines should have been replaced much earlier</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A factory replaced its old machines with new ones of the same capacity. Output per day stayed the same, the number of workers stayed the same, and the number of units rejected by quality control fell from 6 in 100 to 1 in 100.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Which of the following is the best inference from the given facts?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Output, workers and capacity are all unchanged.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">What changed is </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">how much of the output is usable</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> —</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">from 94 in 100 to 99 in 100.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">So the same work now yields more good units.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 2 is contradicted — output per day is the same </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 3 is never mentioned </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 4 is a judgement about the past </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 1</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "3", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50057", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image016.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"130\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image017.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"130\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image018.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"130\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image019.png\" width=\"130\" height=\"130\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": "  <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A square sheet of paper is folded along the dotted line, folded once more along the next dotted line, and a single hole is then punched through the folded sheet, as shown.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Select the answer figure that shows how the sheet will look when it is opened out fully.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><img src=\"https://static-appxdb-v2.akamai.net.in/website/bulk_uploader_images/1792671746739_image015.png\" width=\"353\" height=\"102\" alt ></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Work </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">backwards</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, opening one fold at a time.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The punch goes through two thicknesses of the second fold.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Opening that fold gives </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">two holes</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">,</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">mirror images about the </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">vertical</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> centre line.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Opening the first fold doubles them again,</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">mirror images about the </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">horizontal</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> centre line.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Four holes in all, one in each quarter</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">,</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">each the same distance from the two edges nearest to it.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Options 1 and 2 show only two holes — one fold left unopened </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Option 4 puts the holes </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">on the fold lines</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">,</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">which cannot happen, because the punch was not made on a fold </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✘</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50058", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Only assumption I is implicit</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Only assumption II is implicit</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Both assumptions I and II are implicit</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Neither assumption I nor assumption II is implicit</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A statement is given, followed by two assumptions numbered I and II. An assumption is something taken for granted in the statement. Decide which of the assumptions is implicit in the statement.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Statement: An advertisement reads: “Join our evening batch and clear the examination this year.”</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Assumptions:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">I. Some candidates are looking for coaching outside office hours.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">II. No candidate can clear the examination without coaching.</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Assumption I.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">An </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">evening</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> batch is offered to people</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">who are not free during the day.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The advertisement takes that for granted.</span><br><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Implicit.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Assumption II.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The advertisement praises its own batch;</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">it does not take for granted that every other</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">route is closed. Too strong.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Not implicit.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 1 – Only assumption I is implicit</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "1", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50059", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">He should be promoted</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">He should not be promoted, as a proceeding was begun against him</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">He should not be promoted, as his reports are not good enough</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The case should be kept pending until a fourth report is available</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A clerk is promoted if he satisfies all of the following:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(i) has completed five years of service in the present grade;</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(ii) has an average annual report of 'Good' or better in the last three years;</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">(iii) has no disciplinary proceeding pending.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Case: Mohan completed six years in his grade. His last three reports read Good, Very Good and Good. A disciplinary proceeding begun against him two years ago was closed last year with no charge proved.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">What should be done in his case?</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Check the three conditions one by one.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Service</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — six years, which is at least five </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✔</span><br><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Reports</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — Good, Very Good and Good </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✔</span><br><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Disciplinary proceeding</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\"> — the condition asks whether one is</span><br><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">pending</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">. His was </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">closed</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">, with no charge proved </span><span style=\"font-family:'Symbol'\">✔</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">All three are satisfied.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">A closed proceeding is not a pending one.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 1 – He should be promoted</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}, {"answer": "4", "correct_score": "1", "deleted": "0", "difficulty_level": "0", "id": "50060", "negative_score": "1", "option_1": {"en": "<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4, 1, 3, 2, 5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_2": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5, 1, 4, 2, 3</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_3": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3, 1, 5, 2, 4</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_4": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3, 1, 4, 2, 5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "option_5": "", "option_image_1": "", "option_image_2": "", "option_image_3": "", "option_image_4": "", "option_image_5": "", "question": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Select the correct order of the following words as they would appear in an English dictionary.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">1. Merchant</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">2. Mercy</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3. Mercenary</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">4. Mercury</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">5. Merge</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "question_image": "", "quiz_id": "cgl-2026-tier2-mock9-hindi", "solution_heading": "", "solution_image": "", "solution_text": {"en": " <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Compare the words letter by letter from the left.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">The dictionary order is:</span><br><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Mercenary → Merchant → Mercury → Mercy → Merge</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">By their numbers that is </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">3, 1, 4, 2, 5</span><span style=\"font-family:'Cambria Math'\">.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:4pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;font-family:'Cambria Math'\">Answer: Option 4 – 3, 1, 4, 2, 5</span></p>", "hi": ""}, "solution_video": "", "sortingparam": "0.00"}]}